# AmBot release notes template

## AmBot @VERSION@

First qualified AmBot release candidate for classic Amiga systems.

### Highlights

- AmigaOS 2.04+ and Motorola 68000 baseline
- multi-network IRC sessions
- CAP negotiation and SASL PLAIN
- ARexx command API and event hooks
- persistent configuration and ARexx modules
- optional AmBNC integration and delegated TLS transport
- bounded per-network failure handling
- standalone operation; AmBNC and future BotWeb/PBMP remain optional

### Qualification

This release must be built from the exact binary qualified by M9.2. The
release archive and binary are SHA-256 bound to their manifests and pass the
M9.3 archive audit before publication.

### Licensing

AmBot software is MIT licensed. No Kickstart ROM, AmigaOS/Workbench material,
credentials, private keys or local qualification evidence is included.
